WEBVTT

00:02:56.871 --> 00:03:00.204
Normally what makes a script hot is if
there's a huge celebrity attached

00:03:00.204 --> 00:03:02.288
or if it's a remake of something beloved,

00:03:02.288 --> 00:03:06.829
or if your last movie won six Academy
Awards and grossed a billion dollars,

00:03:07.038 --> 00:03:09.996
you know, and not that those will
stop getting scripts attention,

00:03:09.996 --> 00:03:11.454
I'm sure those guys will
keep getting sold.

00:03:11.496 --> 00:03:14.163
But what's really amazing about what
Franklin did is he managed to find

00:03:14.163 --> 00:03:15.788
another way to get scripts attention.

00:03:16.371 --> 00:03:19.663
If enough of the people who read scripts
all day say that this one,

00:03:19.663 --> 00:03:20.829
this one deserves attention.

00:03:21.496 --> 00:03:22.246
Well, now all of a sudden,

00:03:22.246 --> 00:03:24.413
people actually read it and people
would take it seriously.

00:03:24.954 --> 00:03:27.204
And whatever industry you work in,
whatever you do.

00:03:27.621 --> 00:03:31.079
The question that Franklin's experience
with the blacklist raises is,